# Networking / filesystem USE tuning for the hardened minimal worker.

# cifs-utils: drop `acl` so we don't drag in the whole net-fs/samba stack (and
# its net-libs/ngtcp2[gnutls] QUIC dependency) onto a hardened k8s worker.
# mount.cifs — all we need to mount the backup shares — is always built; the
# acl helpers (get/setcifsacl, which need libsmbclient from samba) are not
# required. Keeps the attack surface + image size down.
net-fs/cifs-utils -acl

# If you DO need CIFS ACL helpers, drop the line above and instead allow:
#   net-libs/ngtcp2 gnutls
# which lets net-fs/samba (pulled by cifs-utils[acl]) resolve.

# NetworkManager is built WITH wifi (capability compiled in, runtime-blocked by
# rfkill/blacklist unless ENABLE_WIFI=true) → it pulls net-wireless/wpa_supplicant,
# which NetworkManager drives over D-Bus, so wpa_supplicant needs [dbus]. emerge's
# --autounmask-continue did not apply this on its own; pre-seed it explicitly.
net-wireless/wpa_supplicant dbus
